The change breaks explicit `!!int` tags for negative binary literals: `[-+]?0b[0-1]+` was replaced with `[^-+]?0b[0-1]+`, so `-0b101` no longer matches the explicit pattern and now throws instead of resolving to `-5`.

```json
{"defect": true, "testFile": {"path": "test/core/proof.test.mjs", "content": "import { describe, it } from 'node:test';
import assert from 'node:assert';
import { load } from 'js-yaml';

describe('proof', () => {
  it('fails on the patched build', () => {
    assert.strictEqual(load('!!int "-0b101"'), -5);
  });
});
"}, "note": "The explicit integer pattern for the core int tag was changed from '[-+]?0b[0-1]+' to '[^-+]?0b[0-1]+', so explicitly tagged negative (or positive) binary literals like '!!int "-0b101"' no longer resolve and now throw a YAMLException instead of returning -5."}
```

